            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0881" n="761" xml:id="pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-18T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 18—11:25
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>231. Department’s 148, October 17, 5 p.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d551-f1"/> Evasive
                    reply received from Foreign Office states Italian Government has no objection to
                    United States inviting Powers mentioned to give their assent to the proposals
                    contained in Department’s 56, May 4, 2 p.m., to [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >via?</hi>] Paris<anchor n="10" xml:id="d551-f2"/> and 107, July 25, 2 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d551-f3"/> Effort
                    being made to secure definite assurance of adherence to proposals outlined in
                    Department’s 148, October 27 [<hi rendition="#italic">17</hi>], 5 p.m. via
                    Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
